# What this corpus draws no page for. One entry per line -- a basename
# for a program that produces no page at all, a basename and " pN" for
# one page of a program that produces others -- each with the reason it
# draws nothing.
#
# A program that draws nothing is outside every comparison a run makes,
# so a run of programs that all drew nothing reports exactly what a run
# in which every one rendered reports: it reached them either way.
# Saying so here in advance is what keeps that from passing for a
# result. An absence nobody declared fails the corpus, and so does a
# declared absence that turns out to have rendered -- the entry's reason
# has lapsed, and the line is left telling its next reader something
# untrue.
#
# Nothing here draws no page. Every program of this corpus is one
# illustration and produces it, the four that never ask for it
# included.
